#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e82e8b16-51a8-59c8-9ed1-51619335de97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pseudoinverse of a Matrix Given Its Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b4a3be8-df10-5faf-b317-36ff32669597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371792} {:answer/id #uuid "d3753217-52ac-503e-a3b9-b9c996fbce84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371793} {:answer/id #uuid "57f72ceb-0f4d-5765-9c5f-222b4acb12bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371794} {:answer/id #uuid "aa40830a-cf56-5825-8289-12a0609ab711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371795} {:answer/id #uuid "1626cc32-b3e1-51e6-9c3b-cf5ddc6a9040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3753217-52ac-503e-a3b9-b9c996fbce84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371793} :answer-field/id #uuid "a85e91e9-8965-591e-9ea0-966d0f58979b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371791}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "acee5e61-29a9-5109-9401-92b3f77d7707" :question/math-academy-id "q-138518" :question/problem "$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162089 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e82e8b16-51a8-59c8-9ed1-51619335de97" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pseudoinverse of a Matrix Given Its Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfb7fc23-b8e2-5ae0-8dca-792bd6119d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388547} {:answer/id #uuid "218a8948-a12b-5a5c-806b-f3b843de42ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388548} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2b2e32-33fa-535d-ab62-422442e91cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388549} {:answer/id #uuid "b231b2f2-252a-5725-bdc3-79d8c48cdc67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388550} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ce7650-d0db-5d82-9e4c-8f0a4f627e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b231b2f2-252a-5725-bdc3-79d8c48cdc67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388550} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b46c685-cbbf-50cd-97a5-b62999fcce5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5dda960b-69e5-5ef3-bb01-a043422ae94b" :question/math-academy-id "q-138534" :question/problem "$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}5\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nV\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of $Σ.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\nV=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}^{+}=\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & =V\\,{Σ}^{+}\\,{U}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{50}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162091 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff858037-da99-53e9-acdc-e4963e7d765e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pseudoinverse of a Matrix Given Its Reduced Singular Value Decomposition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "036b16b2-137c-5e2d-9538-c4642f4bfabd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388561} {:answer/id #uuid "718f7acb-56f9-5179-8b11-19494c3d84e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388562} {:answer/id #uuid "6d990096-dec5-5343-8aa6-bade8f84f6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388563} {:answer/id #uuid "f658c984-c294-56fb-ac55-41e342ac9068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388564} {:answer/id #uuid "125f5671-0146-528e-9023-49616d2c65e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d990096-dec5-5343-8aa6-bade8f84f6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388563} :answer-field/id #uuid "e56d5d22-7464-5aeb-b837-bb4aca5b8269" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388560}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ccd15e93-fc94-54ae-b632-ce7df7380590" :question/math-academy-id "q-138656" :question/problem "$$\n{U}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{V}_{r}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ find the pseudoinverse ${A}^{+}.$" :question/worked-solution "If $A={U}_{r}{Σ}_{r}{V}_{r}^{T}$ is a reduced singular value decomposition of $A,$ then the pseudoinverse of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${Σ}_{r}^{+}$ is the pseudoinverse of ${Σ}_{r}.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n{V}_{r}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{U}_{r}^{T}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{+} & ={V}_{r}\\,{Σ}_{r}^{+}\\,{U}_{r}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
